Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:51:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ember logo: Forge Desktop's ink and copper; whole in narrow
 panes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- The F-and-cube mark takes Forge Desktop's colours, per background: the
  F in ink (paper on dark), the cube's top copper over an ink (paper)
  face and a warm grey one. The brand role (wordmark, keys, prompt mark,
  status glyph) is the same copper.
- A pane 41 to 57 columns wide (a desktop's side terminal) shows the small
  logo, its keys two to a line, instead of none.
- Lines beside the logo never wrap (a wrapped line opened a gap in it):
  the endpoint and the folder keep their ends (`…/live/proj`).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NYxCfae2TEE9hkXEzRbW6j
